statement:
Assume SlicingTheorem. Let P, m ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, and let T ∈ D_{m+1}(U) be integer multiplicity with M_W(T) < ∞ and M_W(∂T) < ∞ for every open W ⊂⊂ U. Then there are currents X_k ∈ D_{m+1}(ℝ^P) (k ∈ ℕ) such that:
- each X_k is integer multiplicity;
- M(X_k) + M(∂X_k) < ∞;
- for every ω ∈ D^{m+1}(U), regarded as a test form on ℝ^P via testFormOnInclusion, X_k(ω) = T(ω) for all sufficiently large k.
